WEBVTT

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.220
It was built as a hotel during the
years of the bubble economy,

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.250
but it was abandoned after that.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.520
It's known as "Battleship Island. "

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.760
This is the area of Team Potemkine.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:46.290
So we're really going, right?

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.400
Actually, I don't think we're gonna
make it over there without a boat.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.160
Whoa! Hey, check it out!

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.540
The tide went out and a path appeared!

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.280
All right, let's go!

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.180
H-Hey!

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.270
Wait up!

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.520
Are we really going?

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.320
I seriously think we shouldn't.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.660
As long as my dear Kazu is going, I don't care

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.360
if it's Battleship Island or
Onigashima Island, I'm there!

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.730
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:22.900
I can't believe Ikki was appointed
the leader of Genesis!

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:30.910
You said it then: that you would take
hold of everything and fly!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.970
I believe in those words of yours!

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.740
Give us the wings!

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:39.840
And lay a path to a new era!

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.220
The new era of Genesis!

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.360
My Sky King!

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.190
I'm just E-Class...

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:57.100
There are so many people out there who can
ride better and fly higher than me...

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.630
So why me?

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.100
Did you know this, Little Crow?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:06.340
When a bird flies too high it dies while flying.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.840
So I want you to be the sky.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.520
A sky that's endlessly high and vast,

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.320
where any bird can fly high and free!

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.330
Ikki...

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.240
Try to imagine what Mega Storm
is there to do as Genesis!

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:35.540
Just try, even if only a little...

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.690
Looks like no one's here.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.430
What the hell is that?!

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.130
What is your business here?

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.870
Oh, actually you must be one of
the members of Potemkine.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.090
Ouch!

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.340
Hey, you!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.610
I was talking to the crow head over there.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.650
He multiplied!

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.080
Ikki Minami.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.480
Or rather...

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.910
Petit Sky King.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.720
That's the ultra-fast-traveling
afterimage body-doubles!

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.550
Why are you so surprised?

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.120
We're just octuplets.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.890
Actually, that makes it more surprising.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.760
It is absolutely meaningless
to do a battle like this.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.570
Crow, I thought you were sharper than that...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.250
So anyway, Crow...

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:22.410
What are you going to do
about Simca's proposal?

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.150
She said she put Genesis into motion, but...

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.420
It doesn't really make much sense, does it?

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.590
What do you think about that, Ringo?

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:33.960
Oh, she's not here...

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.190
Huh? She didn't come?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.700
I'm not sure if it has anything to
do with that Genesis thing,

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.530
but we've been receiving tons
of Parts War challenges.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.870
Man, are you serious?

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:47.200
With the leader of the E-Class team
Kogarasumaru becoming the head of Genesis,

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.180
I'm sure there will be a lot of upstart teams

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:51.010
who'd like to take the opportunity to
slay some of the higher class teams.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.170
Hey, what are YOU doing here anyway?

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:56.320
Just as I explained it to you before,

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.550
Genesis exists only to make
the tower of Tropaeum fall.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:03.220
So as long as you're acting as the leader
of such an enormous organization,

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:07.760
we can't stress how important it is
for you to become an A-Class

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.860
or at least B-Class team.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.160
That's easy enough for you to say!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:15.460
In order for us to get up to B-Class...

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:16.600
Let's see...

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:20.680
You must win three battles in a row in the
quickest course that's high-risk and high-return.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:23.610
If you choose to do it the regular way,
you must win NINE battles in a row.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.650
That's no fun.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.520
Huh?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:32.210
I'm not down with only battling people
who challenge US. It sucks!

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.680
Then what do you want to do?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.960
WE'LL decide who we battle with.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.790
Kazu, tell me which team in this area
still hasn't sent us a challenge yet.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.130
Let's see...

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.760
This E-Class team named "Potem-something"
has never contacted us before.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.000
Potemkine of Battleship Island? I see.

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.240
All right, that's it.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.570
Huh?!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.750
Parts War?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.380
Yeah. Let's do it.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.850
I'm afraid we'll have to refuse.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.490
I'm afraid we don't have any
reason to battle against you.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.620
I'm afraid we don't need any territory
other than this island.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.960
I'm afraid we don't mind
remaining E-Class at all.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.390
We're afraid we must ask you to leave.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.500
Let's get out of here.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.060
I was never interested in this to begin with.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.830
Hey, wait right there, fatass!

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.710
What made you think you're in charge?!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.200
I am the leader, damn it!

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.110
We're going to bet on the fang regalia.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:44.250
Don't you think you've been pushing
your luck a bit too far lately?

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:49.190
Listen. The fang regalia is Agito's...
No, our team's...

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:53.530
No, the entire AT world's...
GREATEST, IRREPLACEABLE ASSET!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:58.600
It is NOT something to be bet on some
cheap battle you want to do on a whim!

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.510
Who would've thought that they'd pick the
unsinkable ship Potemkine as their opponent?

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:05.870
Do you think they'll accept their challenge?

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.350
Supposedly they're not
interested in the Parts War.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.750
But they ARE interested in the regalia.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:16.460
Parts War! E-Class battle, "the Hurdle"!

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:21.060
The course runs about 4.5 kilometers
around Battleship Island.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:27.530
The team of the first person to
cross the finish line wins.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:33.200
When it comes to battle, it is a soldier's
courtesy to exert all his powers at all times.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.540
I don't have time for this.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:37.280
I'm out of here.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.610
Hey, Buccha!

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.020
What?!

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:45.040
No way! We don't have Agito,
and now Buccha is out?!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.920
Oh, wait.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:51.220
Hey, uh, Kogarasumaru has never run this
course, so they're at a disadvantage.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:53.930
Can they just run the course
once as practice today,

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.900
and reschedule the battle for a later date?

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.970
Listen to you. You sound like a
skilled team manager or something.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.760
Oh, it's not like that... But I'd love
to be my dear Kazu's personal manager.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.700
Fine.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:06.100
Then go right ahead.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.600
Kazu, go for a round.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.870
Okay.

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:11.840
Start!

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.110
Go!
Good luck, Kazu!
Kick their asses!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.530
Crap, this is going to be trickier than I thought.

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.660
It puts whoever's behind at a big disadvantage
since the front runner will set the boats rocking.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:42.710
If I trip over and slide off the course
I'll fall into the slimy water,

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.680
and swell up like a lotus root!

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.010
And to make matters worse, I can't even...

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:55.780
Hey, hey, hey!

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.760
What's with this totally unrealistic jump?!

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.420
No one could make it over
there even with ATs on!

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.430
No way!

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:08.470
A double-stage jump?!

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.160
So that's the strategy for beating this course!

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.710
There may be mountains of dead
bodies and rivers of blood,

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.980
but if he can save one life and
contribute to one victory,

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.680
then a soldier's desires are satisfied!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.920
And that is the Potemkine Road, Neclord!

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.320
Holy shit...

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:41.700
What?!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.000
Don't give me that bullshit!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.560
You know damn well I can't swim!

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.410
What?!

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:50.000
My dear Kazu can't swim?!

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.870
How am I supposed to overcome
that Battleship Island?

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.070
I'm sure that's the least of Ikki's concerns...

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.330
What does he think of his team anyway?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.870
She's running again?

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:35.750
It's not like I've always liked
running since I was a kid.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.120
Because it's tiring and it makes me sweat.

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:44.560
Besides, the whole "push-your-limits"
attitude is kinda corny to me.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.670
What am I doing, buying stuff like this?

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.070
What do you think of THIS?

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.750
THE device for a successful love relationship!

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.990
"Sacrifice Power Stone! "

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.250
What the heck is that?

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:09.720
Seriously, this is the bomb! I'm telling you!

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.190
Yeah, sure it works. Look at the
"models" that they're using.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:13.690
Well, different strokes for different folks, I guess.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.030
Hey, have you heard about
Nakaboshi from Class 2?

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.230
Ever since she bought it,

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:18.830
things have been really heating up with
Tamura from the basketball club and...

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.170
Who's that?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.340
Supposedly she's the hottest chick in our grade.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.010
Excuse me, Mikura.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:36.240
Huh?

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:40.280
This... is something I made
during cooking class today.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:44.250
They're sandwiches... You think
you'd be willing to try them?

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.520
This is totally embarrassing!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.130
Thanks, but no thanks. I ate already.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:50.870
S-S-Sorry! Of course you ate already...

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.300
You're so mean! Mikura, you jerk!
Why would you say it like that?

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:56.100
Hey, Kazu, you should eat it! In fact
I'll eat them if you don't...

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.440
Oh, shut up...

00:12:57.440 --> 00:13:02.440
Do you mind if I start calling you
"Kazu-kun" just like the other guys?

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:05.380
No, you can call me Kazu, instead of Kazu-kun.

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:08.310
Good for you, Icchan! Come on, call him Kazu!

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:10.970
H-Hey, Emiri...

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.480
Whoa! Hot!

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.090
I-It's choking my neck...

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.380
I know...

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.990
I already know that wearing a
stupid thing like this won't...

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.870
K-Kazu!

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.290
This...

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:32.770
Oh, this? Well...

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:39.270
Aren't you supposed to wear that on
your wrist, not on your neck?

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:43.040
Huh? Oh, I see! No wonder it was too tight.

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.350
Let me take it off for you.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.290
Wait a second... Wait a second...

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.980
Does this mean...

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.730
Hey, Adachi...

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.220
You run in the morning, right?

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:58.900
I do my AT-ride in the morning,
too, so I see you around a lot.

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:01.460
O-Oh, is that right?

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.930
So why are you in the Track Club?

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.230
Well, 'cuz...

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:07.940
I don't know!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.340
This is amazing! So amazing!
It's working already!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.680
The power of this stone is unbelievable!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.690
I got to be all alone with my dear
Kazu, just like I wanted!

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:30.620
What were you doing, getting
all over Kazu like that?

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:34.660
Ishiwatari said you've gotten
on her nerves big time!

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.670
So that's how she is, huh?

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:42.910
Catch!

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:46.000
I'm gonna dump this stupid thing
in the sewer out back!

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.440
Give it back!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.180
Why are you in the Track Club?

00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:59.420
I don't have a reason.

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:03.000
But I know one day my dear
Kazu will tell me this,

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.490
as he gives me a pat on the head...

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.270
"You just run with your heart and soul,

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.710
and try to catch the wind
with your own two legs..."

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:16.270
"l don't think you need to
have a reason for that. "

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.480
So it's okay...

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:33.850
I don't need a stone like that,

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:36.800
because one day I'll make
it happen with my own legs...

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:40.940
Kazu?!

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.500
What are you two doing? You need
to be nice to each other!

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.080
Crap!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.880
Oh yeah, Kazu can't swim!

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:00.050
Kazu!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.820
Nice toss!

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.430
Thank you! You're a lifesaver!

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:09.490
Here.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.430
That thing's important to you, right?

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:16.590
No...

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.330
But...

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:25.440
But it became so important just now!

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:30.170
Huh? The fang regalia?

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:34.010
Well, either way Agito can't ride right now.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:37.020
And he left the fang regalia with Ikki for now,

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:38.360
so he said you guys are in charge.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:43.080
It'll be fine! You guys are on fire right now!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:45.800
But I'm worried.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.470
The Potemkines... They
appear to be disinterested,

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.570
but they remain on Battleship Island

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.110
so that they can act as agents
for some crooked business

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.340
that has acquired the possessory
right of the property rights

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:57.900
and has been extorting money
from the government...

00:16:58.010 --> 00:16:59.240
Huh...

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:02.370
If they ever manage to get their
hands on the fang regalia,

00:17:02.720 --> 00:17:05.740
I'm certain that they're going
to make a lot of money on it.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:09.440
You say you're not interested, but
I see you've done your homework.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.820
Well, I'm just...

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.760
Isn't Ikki gonna take a shower?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.200
H-Hey!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.000
X-ray vision!

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:23.900
There isn't even a peephole! Give it a rest!

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:30.780
When it comes to the power of my Smell Road,
a thin wall like this has nothing on me!

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:32.480
Whoa! I can see it, too!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:36.440
I can see what's going on in the next room
thanks to Onigiri's telepathic power!

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:40.010
You wish!

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:45.380
But anyway, what the hell IS Ikki thinking?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:49.620
I have no clue why we're fighting this next battle.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.730
Kazu, do you know why?

00:17:51.930 --> 00:17:53.260
I think...

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:56.770
The truth is I doubt even Ikki knows why himself.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:01.240
Someone just walked up to him out of the blue
and asked him to be the head of Genesis,

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.770
but I don't think it really hit him right off the bat.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.530
Then why?

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.950
What are you looking at, Ikki?

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:22.090
There are many different roads in front of you.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.460
They're all possibilities that
you've opened for yourself,

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.630
but which road are you thinking about taking?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.340
Roads, huh?

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.400
Am I seeing them? I wonder.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:41.880
Brrr, it's cold.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:46.310
That's 'cuz you're dressed too light.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:55.150
I think there's nothing in this
world that doesn't change.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:18:59.630
I guess you have to change yourself first

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:05.630
in order to climb to the top with
everyone and realize big dreams...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.500
But you know, you're different, Ikki.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.450
And you're capable of changing
not just yourself,

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:15.880
but those who are around you
as well by wrestling down

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:19.940
and jumping over the enemies that rush
at you and even reality itself...

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.650
I know you have that kind of power.

00:19:24.660 --> 00:19:27.350
And don't you ever forget that.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.120
Ringo...

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:37.030
Nooooo!

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.340
Parts War, E-Class!

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:47.570
We're ready!

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.340
So the three of you are here to battle?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.250
Very well.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:55.080
Then three of us will take your challenge!

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:59.290
The Parts War starts now!

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.390
Go!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.400
Kazu!

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:13.230
Why do I run?

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:15.640
What else is there to do right now?

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.840
We've only just started to run.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.680
There's no way we could run on rails
that have been laid out already!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:30.620
If Ikki runs, we run, too! That's all there is to it!

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:36.260
This will end right here, Kogarasumaru!

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.620
The fang regalia is OURS!

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:40.960
Onigiri!

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:43.470
I got it!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.700
Alrighty!

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.810
Go, Ikki!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:48.900
Yeah!

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.640
What the?!

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:56.940
Maybe you can't reach the goal without
sacrificing your own men,

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.150
but that's not how WE do it!

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.550
That's right! Go, Ikki!

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:07.890
Yessss!

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:24.740
This is quite a disappointment...

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:29.920
Thanks, Adachi!

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:40.160
Kazu!

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.060
Huh?

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:44.360
Too bad I didn't get to see your ass drown!

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:49.130
You jerk!

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:51.200
Jerk!

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:30.370
It's time for our school trip!
Kyoto, here we come!

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:33.600
Sounds like Akito won't be able to go
because he hasn't saved money for it.

00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:35.880
But what's the point of a school trip
if everyone doesn't get to go?

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:38.180
I will retrieve Akito's bankbook from Wanijima!

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:40.770
That's dangerous! I don't think it's possible!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:42.540
I can't just leave Akito alone!

00:23:42.950 --> 00:23:45.320
If we go, every member of
Kogarasumaru has to go!

00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:49.580
Next time on Air Gear...
Operation: Recover Akito's Bankbook!

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:53.120
The hunter of the city starts
wriggling in the darkness!
